{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqenc9e44v4","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"merge_attempt silently no-ops when worker never git commits its worktree","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: a background worker that finishes its task and calls complete_task does NOT automatically commit its worktree changes. If the dispatch prompt omits an explicit \"git commit before complete_task\" step, the attempt branch tip stays equal to the base, the files remain as uncommitted working-tree changes in the worktree dir, and merge_attempt returns {merged:true, head:&lt;unchanged&gt;} — a SILENT no-op. Nothing lands on main. Symptom seen on the handoff-hardening tasks (6d052e96…/1 and /3): two merge_attempt calls both returned the SAME head as current main; ls of the expected new dir showed it missing. Recovery: git -C &lt;worktree&gt; add -A && commit onto the orch/attempt/&lt;key&gt; branch, THEN re-run merge_attempt (head then advances). FIX FORWARD: worker dispatch prompts must carry a third git duty — commit all changes before complete_task — OR merge_attempt should warn/refuse when the branch tip == base (no commits to merge). Verify a merge by checking the returned head actually advanced, not just merged:true.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T03:21:20.524Z","vec":[-0.034693095833063126,-0.04416070878505707,0.0649370327591896,0.029765114188194275,0.0602249875664711,-0.12909799814224243,0.004580386448651552,0.021668395027518272,0.06641294062137604,0.03314439207315445,0.058101922273635864,0.003672867314890027,-0.057790834456682205,0.025245441123843193,-0.03527623042464256,-0.03417086973786354,-0.014250408858060837,0.002270056400448084,-0.025731690227985382,0.031801383942365646,-0.08055359870195389,0.07621317356824875,0.0594974011182785,0.055346399545669556,0.06378964334726334,-0.021547876298427582,-0.10773378610610962,-0.03418901935219765,-0.0342794768512249,-0.030363313853740692,0.0012735864147543907,0.03669928386807442,-0.021267374977469444,0.0404342